<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices up on increased demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices up on increased demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady on Thursday on good demand, dealers said. They said trade was brisk with a firm undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited supply and good demand, they said. Soyoil solvent was up by 300 rupees and soyoil refined rose by 200 rupees per tonne on Thursday.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in dull trade, dealers said. Soymeal yellow was $270 per tonne in export and rapeseed extraction was $134 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,550 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,500 to 4525 FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
